# requirements/kernel/experiment-lifecycle.ears
capability: Experiment lifecycle and runner
owner: kernel
requirements:
  - id: KRN-004
    pattern: event
    text: "When an experiment starts, the kernel shall record input artifact ids with checksums, code revision, environment digests, backend, numerical policies and seed in the manifest."
    rationale: "A verdict must be re-derivable from recorded inputs and environment."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_manifest::test_manifest_is_stored_at_its_logical_path"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_manifest::test_records_inputs_environment_and_seed"
  - id: KRN-005
    pattern: event
    text: "When a compute task completes, the kernel shall write a checkpoint and emit CheckpointWritten."
    rationale: "Multi-hour runs must survive interruption without recomputation."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestExecutor::test_runs_every_task_and_checkpoints_each"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_run_experiment::test_every_completed_task_writes_a_checkpoint"
  - id: KRN-006
    pattern: event
    text: "When an interrupted experiment is resumed, the kernel shall continue from the last checkpoint without re-executing completed tasks."
    rationale: "Resume semantics are tested in the kernel, not delegated (ADR-012)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestExecutor::test_skips_tasks_the_sink_already_holds"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_run_experiment::test_resume_continues_from_last_checkpoint"
  - id: KRN-007
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a compute task fails, then the kernel shall preserve the manifest, diagnostics and partial outputs and mark the experiment Failed."
    rationale: "Failures are evidence too; nothing is discarded."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestExecutor::test_task_errors_surface_as_task_failed_with_diagnostics"
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_experiment::test_failure_preserves_diagnostics"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_run_experiment::test_task_failure_preserves_manifest_diagnostics_and_partial_outputs"
  - id: KRN-008
    pattern: event
    text: "When validate() returns, the kernel shall persist the validation report and issue a verdict that carries every gate outcome."
    rationale: "Every verdict carries the outcomes it was derived from."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestSyntheticProtocol::test_validate_evaluates_every_predeclared_gate"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_validate_experiment::test_kernel_refuses_a_report_that_disagrees_with_its_gate_evaluation"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_validate_experiment::test_only_completed_experiments_validate"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_validate_experiment::test_validation_persists_report_with_every_gate_outcome"
  - id: KRN-009
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If any blocking gate fails or any oracle used by a gate lacks a verification record, then the kernel shall not issue VERIFIED."
    rationale: "VERIFIED must never rest on a failed gate or an unverified oracle."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_verdict::test_a_verdict_that_does_not_follow_from_its_checks_cannot_be_constructed"
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_verdict::test_blocking_gate_failure_prevents_verified"
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_verdict::test_unverified_oracle_prevents_verified"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_validate_experiment::test_a_wrong_planted_slope_is_rejected"
  - id: KRN-012
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a ComputePlan names a TaskKind without a CPU reference implementation, then the kernel shall reject the plan."
    rationale: "Every TaskKind has a CPU reference implementation (ADR-007)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestSyntheticProtocol::test_every_planned_task_kind_has_a_cpu_reference"
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_plan::test_plan_with_task_kind_lacking_cpu_reference_is_rejected"
  - id: KRN-013
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where the CUDA backend is selected, the kernel shall record driver and CUDA versions and the agreement-test result id in the manifest."
    rationale: "GPU results are admissible only with their environment and agreement evidence."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5-dgx]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_experiment::test_cuda_environment_must_record_driver_cuda_and_agreement"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_manifest::test_cuda_runs_record_driver_cuda_and_agreement"
